# Trivy suppressions for the repository filesystem scan (.github/workflows/security-scan.yml).
# Every entry must carry a justification and be revisited when the underlying advisory changes.
#
# GO-2026-5932 (golang.org/x/crypto/openpgp): the advisory marks the whole openpgp
# package as unmaintained with no fixed version, so any x/crypto version matches.
# event-ingestion never imports an openpgp package (verified with
# `go list -deps ./...` in services/event-ingestion); x/crypto is an indirect
# dependency only. Suppression is module-level false-positive handling, not a
# waived vulnerability.
GO-2026-5932
